# rediacc_ci allowlist golden
# reader: bash:.ci/scripts/lib/blocker-validator.sh::parse_blockered_list
# command: parse_blockered_list <corpus> A B '#'; for k in ${!B[@]}; printf '%s\t%s\n'; LC_ALL=C sort
# projection: pairs
# source: .ci-parity-exempt
# corpus: corpus/ci-parity-exempt.list
# comment-char: #
# corpus-sha256: b1a9532ca7ffd92c36cceb19c4ac5c9731afe5e91bf68d11f529dd2c96bfb48e
# ---
ci-only	probes the release-state sentinels in the R2 bucket, so it needs CLOUDFLARE_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID/CLOUDFLARE_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY; a developer without release credentials gets "Required environment variable 'CLOUDFLARE_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID' is not set" rather than a verdict
